# NOTE on appsettings.Development.json:
# It is intentionally NOT gitignored. It only contains a throwaway local
# PostgreSQL password ("1234") for a database that only exists on this
# machine, and a dev-only JWT signing key — neither is a real secret worth
# protecting. Keeping it committed means the project runs out-of-the-box
# for anyone who clones it and has PostgreSQL running locally.
# appsettings.json (the file that matters for real deployments) only holds
# placeholder values; real values for a real environment should come from
# environment variables or a secret store, never from a committed file.
